    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="0808" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg704"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/1897a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Owing to the present disturbances in Mexico City, I have the honor to request
                    that you send telegraphic instructions to the appropriate customs officials to
                    withhold shipments of arms or munitions of war consigned to Mexico City or any
                    point in the State of Mexico, whether already excepted by the President or not,
                    until I shall again communicate with you. The President is being informed of
                    this request.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
